colon -- colon of a (truncated) dual space
******************************************

  * Usage: 
        Dg = colon(D,g)
        DJ = colon(D,J)
  * Inputs:
      * D, an instance of the type *note DualSpace: (NAGtypes)DualSpace,
      * g, a *note ring element: (Macaulay2Doc)RingElement,
      * J, an *note ideal: (Macaulay2Doc)Ideal,
  * *note Optional inputs: (Macaulay2Doc)using functions with optional inputs,:
      * Tolerance => ..., default value .000001
  * Outputs:
      * an instance of the type *note DualSpace: (NAGtypes)DualSpace,, Dg, DJ

Description
===========

This computes (a part of) the dual space of the dual. See

R. Krone and A. Leykin, "Numerical algorithms for detecting embedded
components.", arXiv:1405.7871

for a description.

