diffOp(Matrix) -- create a differential operator
************************************************

  * Function: *note diffOp: diffOp,
  * Usage: 
        diffOp M
  * Inputs:
      * M, a *note matrix: (Macaulay2Doc)Matrix,, consisting of a single
        column, or a *note ring element: (Macaulay2Doc)RingElement,.
  * Outputs:
      * a *note differential operator: DiffOp,, 

Description
===========

Creates a differential operator from a vector of polynomials in $S =
\mathbb{K}[x_1,\dotsc,x_n][dx_1,\dotsc,dx_n]$. The ring $S$ is obtained from
the ring $R = \mathbb{K}[x_1,\dotsc,x_n]$ by using *note diffOpRing:
diffOpRing,.

+------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : R = QQ[x_1,x_2]                                        |
|                                                            |
|o1 = R                                                      |
|                                                            |
|o1 : PolynomialRing                                         |
+------------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : S = diffOpRing R                                       |
|                                                            |
|o2 = S                                                      |
|                                                            |
|o2 : PolynomialRing                                         |
+------------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : diffOp matrix {{(x_1 * x_2 + 3)*dx_1*dx_2^2}, {dx_2^2}}|
|                                                            |
|o3 = | (x_1x_2+3)dx_1dx_2^2 |                               |
|     |        dx_2^2        |                               |
|                                                            |
|                2                                           |
|o3 : DiffOp in S                                            |
+------------------------------------------------------------+

A *note ring element: (Macaulay2Doc)RingElement, can be used instead of a $1
\times 1$ matrix.

+--------------------------+
|i4 : diffOp (x_1^2*dx_1^2)|
|                          |
|o4 = | x_1^2dx_1^2 |      |
|                          |
|                1         |
|o4 : DiffOp in S          |
+--------------------------+

See also
========

  * *note DiffOp: DiffOp, -- differential operator
  * *note diffOpRing: diffOpRing, -- create and cache the ring of differential
    operators

Ways to use this method:
========================

  * *note diffOp(Matrix): diffOp_lpMatrix_rp, -- create a differential operator
  * "diffOp(RingElement)"
