hilbertFunction(ZZ,DualSpace) -- the Hilbert function
*****************************************************

  * Function: *note hilbertFunction: (Macaulay2Doc)hilbertFunction,
  * Usage: 
        k = hilbertFunction(d,S)
        T = hilbertFunction(S)
        K = hilbertFunction(D,S)
  * Inputs:
      * d, an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,, an integer, or a *note list:
        (Macaulay2Doc)List, of arguments
      * S, an instance of the type *note DualSpace: (NAGtypes)DualSpace,, a
        dual space
  * *note Optional inputs: (Macaulay2Doc)using functions with optional inputs,:
      * Strategy (missing documentation) => ..., default value Default, 
  * Outputs:
      * T, a *note tally: (Macaulay2Doc)Tally,, of dimensions for each degree
      * k, an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,, dimensions
      * K, a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,, of dimensions

Description
===========

This function counts the dimension of the dual space in each degree.  A single
degree can be specified, or a list of degrees.  If no degree is specified, then
a Tally is returned pairing each degree with its dimension.

+-----------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : R = CC[x,y];                                          |
+-----------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : I = (ideal {x,y})^4;                                  |
|                                                           |
|o2 : Ideal of R                                            |
+-----------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : D = zeroDimensionalDual(origin R, I)                  |
|                                                           |
|o3 = | 1 y x .5y2 xy .5x2 .166667y3 .5xy2 .5x2y .166667x3 ||
|                                                           |
|o3 : DualSpace                                             |
+-----------------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : hilbertFunction D                                     |
|                                                           |
|o4 = Tally{0 => 1}                                         |
|           1 => 2                                          |
|           2 => 3                                          |
|           3 => 4                                          |
|                                                           |
|o4 : Tally                                                 |
+-----------------------------------------------------------+

