isPointEmbeddedInCurve(AbstractPoint,Ideal) -- numerically determine if the point is an embedded component of a 1-dimensional scheme
************************************************************************************************************************************

  * Function: *note isPointEmbeddedInCurve:
    isPointEmbeddedInCurve_lpAbstractPoint_cmIdeal_rp,
  * Usage: 
        B = isPointEmbeddedInCurve(P,I)
  * Inputs:
      * P, a *note point: (NAGtypes)AbstractPoint,
      * I, an *note ideal: (Macaulay2Doc)Ideal,
  * *note Optional inputs: (Macaulay2Doc)using functions with optional inputs,:
      * Regularity => ..., default value -1
  * Outputs:
      * B, a *note Boolean value: (Macaulay2Doc)Boolean,

Description
===========

This method runs a numerical embedded component test described in the following
paper.

R. Krone and A. Leykin, "Numerical algorithms for detecting embedded
components.", arXiv:1405.7871

The optional parameter Regularity can be used to set the local Hilbert
regularity. The default value -1 computes it using *note
localHilbertRegularity: localHilbertRegularity,

