localHilbertRegularity -- regularity of the local Hilbert function of a polynomial ideal
****************************************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        d = localHilbertRegularity(p,I)
  * Inputs:
      * p, a *note point: (NAGtypes)AbstractPoint,, 
      * I, an *note ideal: (Macaulay2Doc)Ideal,, or a one-row *note matrix:
        (Macaulay2Doc)Matrix, of generators
  * *note Optional inputs: (Macaulay2Doc)using functions with optional inputs,:
      * *note Tolerance: Tolerance _lpNoetherianOperators_rp, => ..., default
        value null, optional argument for numerical tolerance
  * Outputs:
      * d, an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,, 

Description
===========

The *note g-corners: gCorners, of the ideal are computed in order to find the
Hilbert polynomial, which is compared to the Hilbert function to find the
degree of regularity, which is the degree at which the two become equal.

+--------------------------------------------+
|i1 : R = CC[x,y];                           |
