noetherianOperators(Ideal) -- Noetherian operators of a primary ideal
*********************************************************************

  * Function: *note noetherianOperators: noetherianOperators,
  * Usage: 
        noetherianOperators Q
        noetherianOperators (Q, Strategy => "PunctualQuot")
  * Inputs:
      * Q, an *note ideal: (Macaulay2Doc)Ideal,, assumed to be primary
  * Outputs:
      * a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,, of *note differential operators:
        DiffOp,

Description
===========

Compute a set of Noetherian operators for the primary ideal I.

+----------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : R = QQ[x,y,t];                                 |
+----------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : I = ideal(x^2, y^2-x*t);                       |
|                                                    |
|o2 : Ideal of R                                     |
+----------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : noetherianOperators I                          |
|                                                    |
|o3 = {| 1 |, | dy |, | tdy^2+2dx |, | tdy^3+6dxdy |}|
|                                                    |
|o3 : List                                           |
+----------------------------------------------------+

The optional argument Strategy can be used to choose different algorithms. Each
strategy may accept additional optional arguments, see the documentation page
for each strategy for details.

  * *note "PunctualQuot" (default): Strategy => "PunctualQuot",
  * *note "PunctualHilbert" (alias for "PunctualQuot"): Strategy =>
    "PunctualQuot",
  * *note "MacaulayMatrix": Strategy => "MacaulayMatrix",
  * *note "Hybrid": Strategy => "Hybrid",

Caveat
======

The behavior is undefined if Q is not primary. For non-primary ideals, use
*note noetherianOperators(Ideal,Ideal): noetherianOperators_lpIdeal_cmIdeal_rp,

