noetherianOperators(Ideal,Ideal) -- Noetherian operators of a primary component
*******************************************************************************

  * Function: *note noetherianOperators: noetherianOperators,
  * Usage: 
        noetherianOperators (I, P)
        noetherianOperators (I, P, Strategy => "MacaulayMatrix")
        noetherianOperators (I, P, Rational => false)
  * Inputs:
      * I, an *note ideal: (Macaulay2Doc)Ideal,, 
      * P, an *note ideal: (Macaulay2Doc)Ideal,, a minimal prime of $I$
  * Outputs:
      * a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,, of *note differential operators:
        DiffOp,

Description
===========

Compute a set of Noetherian operators for the $P$-primary component of $I$.

+------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : R = QQ[x,y,t];                                               |
+------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : I1 = ideal(x^2, y^2-x*t);                                    |
|                                                                  |
|o2 : Ideal of R                                                   |
+------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : I2 = ideal((x-t)^2);                                         |
|                                                                  |
|o3 : Ideal of R                                                   |
+------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : I = intersect(I1, I2);                                       |
|                                                                  |
|o4 : Ideal of R                                                   |
+------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i5 : noetherianOperators(I, radical I1)                           |
|                                                                  |
|o5 = {| 1 |, | dy |, | tdy^2+2dx |, | tdy^3+6dxdy |}              |
|                                                                  |
|o5 : List                                                         |
+------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i6 : noetherianOperators(I, radical I2) == noetherianOperators(I2)|
|                                                                  |
|o6 = true                                                         |
+------------------------------------------------------------------+

The optional argument Strategy can be used to choose different algorithms. Each
strategy may accept additional optional arguments, see the documentation page
for each strategy for details.

  * *note "MacaulayMatrix" (default): Strategy => "MacaulayMatrix",
  * *note "Hybrid": Strategy => "Hybrid",

If the prime $P$ is known to be a rational point, the optional argument
Rational can be set to true.  This may offer a speed-up in the computation.

