noetherianOperators(Module,Ideal) -- Noetherian operators of a primary component
********************************************************************************

  * Function: *note noetherianOperators: noetherianOperators,
  * Usage: 
        noetherianOperators (U, P)
  * Inputs:
      * U, a *note module: (Macaulay2Doc)Module,, 
      * P, an *note ideal: (Macaulay2Doc)Ideal,, a minimal prime of comodule U
  * Outputs:
      * a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,, of *note differential operators:
        DiffOp,

Description
===========

Compute a set of Noetherian operators for the $P$-primary component of comodule
U.

+------------------------------------------+
|i1 : R = QQ[x,y,z]                        |
|                                          |
|o1 = R                                    |
|                                          |
|o1 : PolynomialRing                       |
+------------------------------------------+
|i2 : U = image matrix{{x,y,z},{y,z,x}}    |
|                                          |
|o2 = image | x y z |                      |
|           | y z x |                      |
|                                          |
|                             2            |
|o2 : R-module, submodule of R             |
+------------------------------------------+
|i3 : P = first associatedPrimes comodule U|
|                                          |
|o3 = ideal (y - z, x - z)                 |
|                                          |
|o3 : Ideal of R                           |
+------------------------------------------+
|i4 : noetherianOperators(U, P)            |
|                                          |
|o4 = {| -1 |}                             |
|      |  1 |                              |
|                                          |
|o4 : List                                 |
+------------------------------------------+

If there are no embedFded primes, running this command for all associated
primes is equivalent to running a *note differential primary decomposition:
differentialPrimaryDecomposition,.

+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i5 : associatedPrimes comodule U /                                           |
|         (P -> {P, noetherianOperators(U,P)})                                |
|                                                                             |
|                                                            2          2     |
|o5 = {{ideal (y - z, x - z), {| -1 |}}, {ideal (x + y + z, y  + y*z + z ), {||
|                              |  1 |                                        ||
|     ------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|     -z |}}}                                                                 |
|      y |                                                                    |
|                                                                             |
|o5 : List                                                                    |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i6 : netList differentialPrimaryDecomposition U                              |
|                                                                             |
|     +--------------------------------+--------+                             |
|o6 = |ideal (y - z, x - z)            |{| -1 |}|                             |
|     |                                | |  1 | |                             |
|     +--------------------------------+--------+                             |
|     |                   2          2 |        |                             |
|     |ideal (x + y + z, y  + y*z + z )|{| -z |}|                             |
|     |                                | |  y | |                             |
|     +--------------------------------+--------+                             |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+

