numericalNoetherianOperators -- Noetherian operators via numerical interpolation
********************************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        numericalNoetherianOperators(I)
  * Inputs:
      * I, an *note ideal: (Macaulay2Doc)Ideal,, unmixed
  * Outputs:
      * a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,, of *note expressions:
        (Macaulay2Doc)Expression,

Description
===========

The method computes specialized Noetherian operators from many sampled points,
and attempts to find fitting rational functions using rational function
interpolation.

+-----------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : R = CC[x,y,t];                                        |
+-----------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : I = ideal(x^2, y^2 - x*t);                            |
|                                                           |
|o2 : Ideal of R                                            |
+-----------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : numericalNoetherianOperators(I, DependentSet => {x,y})|
|                                                           |
|                 2    1      t   3                         |
|o3 = {1, 1*dy, dy  + ---*dx, -*dy  + 1*dx*dy}              |
|                     .5t     6                             |
|                                                           |
|o3 : List                                                  |
+-----------------------------------------------------------+

The behavior of the function can be adjusted using options. Currently only the
option *note DependentSet: DependentSet, is required. The following are
supported:



TrustedPoint => a *note point: (NAGtypes)AbstractPoint,. The function does not
compute specialized Noetherian operators from scratch for each point. Instead,
it computes it for a "trusted" point on the variety, and uses the obtained
Noetherian operators as a template for the rest of the computation. If
TrustedPoint is unset, the first point returned by the sampler will be used as
the trusted point.

NoetherianDegreeLimit => a non-negative *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,.
Limits the degrees of the Noetherian operators (with respect to the variables
$dx_i$). If unset, will compute the full Noetherian operators of the "trusted"
point. Can introduce speed-ups when the maximal degree of the Noetherian
operators is known in advance.

Tolerance => a positive real number. This specifies the numerical precision
when computing the specialized Noetherian operators. The default value is 1e-6.
See *note Tolerance (NoetherianOperators): Tolerance
_lpNoetherianOperators_rp,.

Sampler => a function, taking inputs (n,I), where I is an *note ideal:
(Macaulay2Doc)Ideal,, and n is an integer. The sampler function returns a list
of n *note points: (NAGtypes)AbstractPoint, on the component of interest of I.
If unset, the default sampler uses *note Bertini: (Bertini)Top,, and assumes
that I is primary.

DependentSet => a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List, of variables that are
algebraically dependent. See *note DependentSet: DependentSet, for details.

InterpolationTolerance => a positive real number. This specifies the numerical
precision for the interpolation routines. The default value is 1e-6. See *note
Tolerance (NoetherianOperators): Tolerance _lpNoetherianOperators_rp,.

InterpolationDegreeLimit => a non-negative *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,.
Limits the degree of the interpolated rational function coefficients. If no
rational functions are found within the degree limit, outputs an incomplete
differential operator

+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : R = CC[x,y,t];                                                          |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : I = ideal(x^2, y^2 - x*t);                                              |
|                                                                             |
|o2 : Ideal of R                                                              |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : numericalNoetherianOperators(I, DependentSet => {x,y},                  |
|                                                                             |
|                   2   ?     ?   3                                           |
|o3 = {1, 1*dy, 1*dy  + -*dx, -*dy  + 1*dx*dy}                                |
|                       ?     ?                                               |
|                                                                             |
|o3 : List                                                                    |
|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|InterpolationDegreeLimit => 0)                                               |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+

See also
========

  * *note rationalInterpolation: rationalInterpolation, -- numerically
    interpolate rational functions

Ways to use numericalNoetherianOperators:
=========================================

  * "numericalNoetherianOperators(Ideal)"

