rationalInterpolation(List,List,Ring) -- numerically interpolate rational functions
***********************************************************************************

  * Function: *note rationalInterpolation: rationalInterpolation,
  * Usage: 
        (n,d) = rationalInterpolation(pts, vals, R)
  * Inputs:
      * pts, a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,, of one-row matrices
        corresponding to points at which the rational function was evaluated
      * vals, a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,, of *note numbers:
        (Macaulay2Doc)Number, corresponding to evaluations of the rational
        function
      * R, a *note ring: (Macaulay2Doc)Ring,, the polynomial ring in which the
        numerator and denominator are sought
  * *note Optional inputs: (Macaulay2Doc)using functions with optional inputs,:
      * *note Tolerance: Tolerance _lpNoetherianOperators_rp, => ..., default
        value .000001, optional argument for numerical tolerance
  * Outputs:
      * n, a *note ring element: (Macaulay2Doc)RingElement,, the numerator of
        the rational function
      * d, a *note ring element: (Macaulay2Doc)RingElement,, the denominator of
        the rational function

Description
===========

Given a list of points $pts = \{p_1,\dots,p_k\}$ and values $vals =
\{v_1,\dots,v_k\}$, attempts to find a rational function $f = g/h$, such that
$f(p_i) = v_i$. The method first tries to find polynomials $g,h$ of degree 0;
if this fails, it tries to find $g,h$ of degree 1 and so on. This procedure
stops when there are not enough points to compute the next degree, in which
case an error will be thrown.

+---------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : R = CC[x]                                                       |
|                                                                     |
|o1 = R                                                               |
|                                                                     |
|o1 : PolynomialRing                                                  |
+---------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : pts = {point{{0}},point{{1}},point{{2}}, point{{3}}, point{{4}}}|
|                                                                     |
|o2 = {{0}, {1}, {2}, {3}, {4}}                                       |
|                                                                     |
|o2 : List                                                            |
+---------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : vals = {-1, 1/2, 1, 5/4, 7/5}                                   |
|                                                                     |
|          1     5  7                                                 |
|o3 = {-1, -, 1, -, -}                                                |
|          2     4  5                                                 |
|                                                                     |
|o3 : List                                                            |
+---------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : rationalInterpolation(pts, vals, R)                             |
|                                                                     |
|o4 = (2x - 1, 1x + 1)                                                |
|                                                                     |
|o4 : Sequence                                                        |
+---------------------------------------------------------------------+

