truncate(DualSpace,List,ZZ) -- truncate a polynomial space or dual space
************************************************************************

  * Function: *note truncate: (Macaulay2Doc)truncate,
  * Usage: 
        S = truncate(T, v, d)
  * Inputs:
      * T, an instance of the type *note DualSpace: (NAGtypes)DualSpace,, or an
        instance of the type *note PolySpace: (NAGtypes)PolySpace,
      * v, a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,, a list of the integers
        designating which variables to bound
      * d, an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,, the degree bound for the
        designated variables
  * Outputs:
      * S, an instance of the type *note DualSpace: (NAGtypes)DualSpace,, 

Description
===========

This method truncates a dual space or polynomial space T, so that the total
degree of the specified variables is bounded by d.

+-------------------------------------------+
|i1 : R = CC[x,y];                          |
+-------------------------------------------+
|i2 : I = ideal {x,y};                      |
|                                           |
|o2 : Ideal of R                            |
+-------------------------------------------+
|i3 : D = zeroDimensionalDual(origin R, I^3)|
|                                           |
|o3 = | 1 y x .5y2 xy .5x2 |                |
|                                           |
|o3 : DualSpace                             |
+-------------------------------------------+
|i4 : truncate(D, {0}, 1)                   |
|                                           |
|o4 = | xy x y2 y 1 |                       |
|                                           |
|o4 : DualSpace                             |
+-------------------------------------------+

Ways to use this method:
========================

  * *note truncate(DualSpace,List,ZZ): truncate_lpDualSpace_cmList_cmZZ_rp, --
    truncate a polynomial space or dual space
  * "truncate(PolySpace,List,ZZ)"
