truncate(DualSpace,ZZ) -- truncate a polynomial space or dual space
*******************************************************************

  * Function: *note truncate: (Macaulay2Doc)truncate,
  * Usage: 
        S = truncate(T, d)
  * Inputs:
      * T, an instance of the type *note DualSpace: (NAGtypes)DualSpace,, or an
        instance of the type *note PolySpace: (NAGtypes)PolySpace,
      * d, an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,, the degree bound for the
        designated variables
  * Outputs:
      * S, an instance of the type *note DualSpace: (NAGtypes)DualSpace,, 

Description
===========

This method truncates a dual space or polynomial space T so that the total
degree of all terms does not exceed d.

+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : R = CC[x,y];                                                            |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : I = ideal {x-y};                                                        |
|                                                                             |
|o2 : Ideal of R                                                              |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : D = truncatedDual(origin R, I, 5)                                       |
|                                                                             |
|o3 = | 1 x+y .5x2+xy+.5y2 .166667x3+.5x2y+.5xy2+.166667y3                    |
|                                                                             |
|o3 : DualSpace                                                               |
|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|.0416667x4+.166667x3y+.25x2y2+.166667xy3+.0416667y4                          |
|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|.00833333x5+.0416667x4y+.0833333x3y2+.0833333x2y3+.0416667xy4+.00833333y5 |  |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : truncate(D, 3)                                                          |
|                                                                             |
|o4 = | x3+3x2y+3xy2+y3 x2+2xy+y2 x+y 1 |                                     |
|                                                                             |
|o4 : DualSpace                                                               |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+

Ways to use this method:
========================

  * *note truncate(DualSpace,ZZ): truncate_lpDualSpace_cmZZ_rp, -- truncate a
    polynomial space or dual space
  * "truncate(PolySpace,ZZ)"
